{"id": "EUVD-2026-48728", "enisaUuid": "ee13e7d9-6676-3a98-905c-1c52f7e5d398", "description": "A flaw was found in the cluster-proxy service-proxy component used in Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management for Kubernetes (RHACM) and multicluster-engine (MCE). The service-proxy appends impersonation group headers to proxied requests without first removing caller-supplied values, and the spoke ServiceAccount holds unrestricted impersonation permissions. An authenticated hub principal can inject an Impersonate-Group header to escalate to cluster-admin on every managed cluster.", "datePublished": "2026-07-24T18:56:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-29T18:42:15", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:46885", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:47388", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:47735", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:47949", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:47953", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:47974", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:48284", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-17107", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2506771"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-17107", "GHSA-vr7g-637m-v9mm"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.57, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "26e87d31-4d95-3ff4-aee9-ccfa6b05d4cb", "product": {"name": "multicluster engine for Kubernetes 2.6", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1783985960"}, {"id": "2abf9679-38f0-3f6a-a846-d9c0b8c91ea3", "product": {"name": "multicluster engine for Kubernetes 2.10", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1784342329"}, {"id": "4353d265-cd16-3c96-adbf-da3b873619c7", "product": {"name": "multicluster engine for Kubernetes 2.8", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1784342329"}, {"id": "a0fd03be-f715-3e07-89e4-95ed038772e5", "product": {"name": "multicluster eng